/// The MemQL Portal, as site #1.
///
/// SEEDED, not special-cased. The portal is how sites are managed, so if it
/// were an ordinary row the cluster would ship with an empty site table and no
/// way to reach the screen that fills it. Seeding resolves that without a
/// branch in the serving path -- and re-seeding at boot means an operator
/// cannot brick cluster management by deleting the row.
///
/// bundleRef is file:///app/portal -- the directory the image already ships
/// and that MEMQL_PORTAL_DIST used to point at (component/portal, retired,
/// memql#3711). That is the whole of the difference between "in the image"
/// and "in storage": a URI scheme.
///
/// status is "live" and systemOwned is true -- createSite's ordinary caller
/// gets "draft" / false; the portal needs both flipped at materialization
/// time, which is why createSite (dsl/platform/mutations.memql) accepts them
/// as optional args instead of hardcoding the operator-created-site defaults.
///
/// The hostname is the ONE thing a customer site gets from the portal UI and
/// the portal gets from the cluster install. It carries the committed default
/// the same way the Ingress hosts do (memql#3593); an install on another
/// domain overrides it through the same seam.
///
/// NO ownerUserId, and its ABSENCE is the meaning (memql#4344): an empty owner
/// is the CLUSTER-OWNED state, which is what site #1 has to be -- the portal is
/// the platform's row, not whichever principal happened to boot the cluster.
/// createSite stamps `ownerUserId: actor.userId` like every owned concept must,
/// and executeWrite undoes that stamp for a system actor, so adding the field
/// here would be both unnecessary and wrong. `portal.<domain>` is also a
/// RESERVED label a user may not claim, and the same privileged path is what
/// lets this seed use it (component/memql/platform_site_hostname_policy.go).
@description("The MemQL Portal as site #1")
seed site portal {
  id:          "portal"
  hostname:    "portal.memql.localhost"
  kind:        "spa"
  bundleRef:   "file:///app/portal"
  status:      "live"
  apiProxy:    true
  systemOwned: true
  title:       "MemQL Portal"
}
